Here’s a proposed structure for your State-of-the-Art React Frontend that aligns with your requirements for a non-commercial academic research prototype:

1. Project Structure
my-quad-gif-generator/
├── public/
│   └── index.html
├── src/
│   ├── components/
│   │   ├── GifPreviewPanel.jsx
│   │   ├── UploadControls.jsx
│   │   ├── LLMSelector.jsx
│   │   ├── ProgressStatus.jsx
│   │   └── DownloadManager.jsx
│   ├── services/
│   │   ├── huggingFaceAPI.js
│   │   └── gifProcessing.js
│   ├── App.jsx
│   ├── index.js
│   └── styles/
│       └── app.css
├── package.json
└── README.md

2. Core Features
Quad-GIF Generator UI
Four simultaneous preview panels for LLM-generated GIFs.
Each panel updates consecutively as generation completes.
Hugging Face Integration
Use the Hugging Face Inference API with a freeware academic hall-pass (token limited to non-commercial research).
huggingFaceAPI.js handles authentication and requests.
Developer-Ready Access
Include .env for storing API keys securely.
Modular React components for easy extension.
Clear inline documentation for academic researchers.
Local Video Editor Upload
Download buttons automatically store GIFs.
Optional upload to a private local video editor folder via File System Access API (browser-supported).

3. Example React Component: GifPreviewPanel.jsx
import React from "react";

const GifPreviewPanel = ({ gifUrl, index }) => {
  return (
    <div className="gif-panel">
      <h3>Preview {index + 1}</h3>
      {gifUrl ? (
        <img src={gifUrl} alt={`Generated GIF ${index + 1}`} />
      ) : (
        <p>Waiting for generation...</p>
      )}
    </div>
  );
};

export default GifPreviewPanel;

4. Hugging Face API Example
// src/services/huggingFaceAPI.js
export async function generateGIFFromPrompt(prompt) {
  const response = await fetch("https://api-inference.huggingface.co/models/YOUR_MODEL", {
    headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.REACT_APP_HF_TOKEN}` },
    method: "POST",
    body: JSON.stringify({ inputs: prompt })
  });
  const result = await response.json();
  return result.gifUrl; // Assume your model returns a gif URL
}

5. Suggested Next Steps
Initialize with create-react-app or Vite.
Integrate Hugging Face free academic key.
Implement 4-panel queue logic for consecutive GIF generation.
Add local download and optional editor upload.



